cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Intent in research or writing, please cite it like this."
title: "Intent: a deterministic compiler from plain English to native code"
abstract: >-
  Intent is an experimental programming language in which a program states what information
  exists and what should be possible with it, in ordinary English sentences. A deterministic
  compiler, with no machine learning in it, chooses data structures and algorithms and emits
  LLVM IR. Unknown words and ambiguous sentences stop compilation with a question instead of
  a guess. A reference interpreter defines the meaning, and the native code is tested against
  it on random commands.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: srivtx
repository-code: "https://github.com/srivtx/intent"
url: "https://intent.srivtx.xyz"
keywords:
  - programming language
  - natural language programming
  - controlled natural language
  - compiler
  - LLVM
  - program synthesis
  - data structure selection
